WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
A real local example: the Web SDK talks to a running Likerts API.

00:04.000 --> 00:09.000
The operator view starts empty. Responses are held in temporary memory.

00:09.000 --> 00:20.800
Answer inside the sample storefront using the actual Web SDK renderer.

00:20.800 --> 00:27.400
The API accepts the answer and returns a real response ID.

00:27.400 --> 00:36.600
Retrieve the stored answer and metadata. The response ID matches the receipt.

00:36.600 --> 00:40.400
Refresh reads the same response. Local memory clears when the demo stops.
